@startuml
title Where a viewer directory is reclaimed, and why not earlier

participant "caller" as C
participant "atexit" as A
participant "multiprocessing.util\n_exit_function" as U
participant "worker" as W

C -> C: show(open_window=False)
note right of C
  Registers the reclaim twice:
  an atexit hook, and a finalizer
  at priority -1 when a worker
  may exist.
end note

C -> A: interpreter exits
A -> A: run hooks, last registered first
A -> A: reclaim: rmdir refused,\nthe worker still holds the viewer
A -> U: _exit_function

group phase 1 -- finalizers at priority >= 0
  U -> U: nothing of ours here\n(that is the point)
end

group phase 2 -- terminate daemons, join every active child
  U -> W: join
  W -> W: unlink the viewer it was handed
  W --> U: exited
end

group phase 3 -- remaining finalizers
  U -> U: reclaim at priority -1:\nthe directory is empty, rmdir succeeds
end

note over U
  A reclaim in phase 1 spends its one
  chance on a directory that is about
  to empty. Negative priority is what
  puts it after the join.
end note
@enduml
